L140: ### Breaking changes
L141: 
L142: The `ubuntu-latest` label is ready to become the default version for Ubuntu 26.04.
L143: ### Target date
L144: 
L145: This change will be rolled out over a period of several weeks beginning October 19, 2026.
L146: We plan to complete the migration by November 19, 2026.
L147: 
L148: ### The motivation for the changes
L149: 
L150: Ubuntu 26.04 has completed its public preview period and is generally available for production workloads.
L151: We have monitored customer feedback and image stability, and are now ready to set it as the latest version for the x64 `ubuntu-latest` label.
L152: ### Possible impact
L153: 
L154: Workflows and pipelines that depend on Ubuntu 24.04-specific software, package versions, system libraries, compilers, or prebuilt binaries may be affected.
L155: ### Software difference between Ubuntu 24.04 and Ubuntu 26.04
L156: Tool name  | Ubuntu 24.04  | Ubuntu 26.04  | Notes
L157: --- | --- | --- | ---
L158: Operating system  | Ubuntu 24.04.5 LTS  | Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS  | New Ubuntu LTS release
L159: Kernel  | 6.17.0-1022-azure  | 7.0.0-1012-azure  | Updated with the new operating system
L160: Systemd  | 255.4-1ubuntu8.17  | 259.5-0ubuntu3.4  | Updated with the new operating system
L161: Docker Buildx  | 0.37.0  | 0.37.0  | Available on both images
L162: Minikube  | 1.39.0  | 1.39.0  | Available on both images
L163: AWS CLI  | 2.36.40  | 2.36.40  | Available on both images
L164: Azure CLI  | 2.90.0  | 2.90.0  | Available on both images
L165: Google Cloud CLI  | 583.0.0  | 583.0.0  | Available on both images
L166: Rust  | 1.98.1  | 1.98.1  | Available on both images
L167: Firefox  | 155.0  | 155.0  | Available on both images
L168: Java  | 17.0.20+1 (default)  | 25.0.5+8 (default)  | Default version updated to Java 25
L169: For the complete list of installed software, see the 【63†Ubuntu 26.04】 image documentation.
